# pdf/src/pdffont.aiw -- a font of a PDF file as what a reader of text
# needs of it (ISO 32000-1, 9.6 to 9.10): which characters a code of a
# string stands for, and how wide its glyph is.
#
#   pdffontmake d a e        the font whose dictionary is at a
#   pdffontnext r p n i      the code at the place i of a string
#   pdffonttext r code b     add the characters of a code, as UTF-8
#   pdffontwidth r code      the width of its glyph, in thousandths
#   pdffontspace r code      whether it is the space of a font of one byte
#   pdffontfree d r          give the font back
#
# d is a document of pdf/src/pdfdoc.aiw, whose memory and work the font
# counts against; pdffontmake returns the address of the font, or 0 if
# the document is spent or the kernel has no memory.
#
# A code is one byte, or two in a font of the subtype Type0. Its
# characters are, in this order of precedence: what the ToUnicode CMap
# of the font says (bfchar and bfrange, with a destination of several
# characters and with surrogate pairs); for a font of one byte, the
# glyph name that the Differences of its Encoding give the code, and
# then its base encoding: WinAnsiEncoding, MacRomanEncoding or
# StandardEncoding if the font names one; if it names none, the
# encoding that a Type 1 font program in the file has in its clear
# part (FontFile; "dup 58 /period put"), as the fonts of TeX need it;
# else StandardEncoding, or WinAnsiEncoding for a TrueType font. A
# glyph name is one of the table below, with what follows a dot left
# out, or uniXXXX, or uXXXX to uXXXXXX, or a name of one byte, which is
# that character. A code with no characters is U+FFFD. The five
# ligatures U+FB00 to U+FB04 are written as their letters.
#
# What is not read: an Encoding of a Type0 font that is not of two
# bytes a code, and the encoding inside a font program that is not of
# Type 1 (FontFile2, FontFile3). A font without ToUnicode that needs
# one of them gives U+FFFD or the characters of its base encoding.
#
# The widths are those of Widths, or of W and DW of the descendant of a
# Type0 font; a font of one byte without Widths has 500 for every code,
# 600 if its name starts with Courier.
#
# Every name of this file starts with "pdffont"; a program has no var
# of such a name (see lib/std/io.aiw).
use "lib/std/bytes.aiw"
use "pdf/src/pdfobj.aiw"
use "pdf/src/pdfdoc.aiw"
use "pdf/src/pdfstm.aiw"

# A font: the address of its dictionary (0), 1 if a code is two bytes
# (8), the table of the codes (16: four bytes a code, the character, or
# with the highest bit the place in the bytes at 32 of several, the low
# 24 bits, and their number, the 7 above), the widths (24: two bytes a
# code), the characters of the codes that have several (32: a buffer
# of lib/std/bytes.aiw) and how many bytes of that buffer were counted
# as memory of the document (56).
const pdffontsize 64

